# Copy to `rates` beside this file and fill in. That file is untracked on
# purpose -- `config` is a symlink into the dotfiles repo, and hourly rates
# do not belong in version control.
#
# Two forms, both read:
#
#   PUNCH_RATE_<NAME>   for ASCII names, uppercased with non-alphanumerics
#                       turned into `_` -- project `client-a` reads
#                       PUNCH_RATE_CLIENT_A
#
#   punch_rate[<tag>]   keyed by the tag exactly as recorded, and the only
#                       form that works for Chinese names: those cannot form
#                       a shell identifier, so every one of them would
#                       otherwise collapse onto the same variable
#
# Anything without a rate still appears in `punch bill`, with no amount --
# unbilled work stays visible rather than being priced at zero.

# PUNCH_RATE_CLIENT_A=2000
# punch_rate[內部工具]=800
